4. THE EXTERNAL FIELD AT THE LOCAL GROUP -- measured from its own peculiar velocity, and why it decides
==============================================================================================================================
  LG peculiar velocity w.r.t. the CMB = 620 km/s; linear theory g_ext = (3/2) H_0 v/f, f = 0.530
  => g_ext (the TRUE field, already boosted) = 3.835e-12 m/s^2
  canonical  g_ext/a_0 = 0.0410 (true)  ->  g_N,ext/a_0 = 0.00161   nu(e_N) =  25.41   L = d ln nu/d ln y = -0.490   G_eff/G = nu(1 - L/3) =  21.26
  alt        g_ext/a_0 = 0.0339 (true)  ->  g_N,ext/a_0 = 0.00111   nu(e_N) =  30.47   L = d ln nu/d ln y = -0.492   G_eff/G = nu(1 - L/3) =  25.47
  canonical  the LG's OWN field at the measured R_0 is H_Lam^2 R_0 = 8.910e-14 m/s^2 = 0.00095 a_0  -- i.e. 43x SMALLER than the external field
  alt        the LG's OWN field at the measured R_0 is H_Lam^2 R_0 = 1.299e-13 m/s^2 = 0.00115 a_0  -- i.e. 30x SMALLER than the external field
  [PASS] K02.5 THE STRUCTURAL FINDING, and it is against the item's own premise: at the turnaround radius the system's internal field is H_Lam^2 R_0 by construction, which for the Local Group is 30-50x below the external field of large-scale structure.  The isolated deep-MOND branch of item 80 is therefore NOT the applicable regime, and this check records that rather than hiding it   (external field exceeds the internal field at R_0 by more than 5x on both footings)

