6. SENSITIVITY AND MUTATION CONTROLS
==============================================================================================================================
  levers on the EFE-quenched prediction R_0 = x_ta (nu(e_N) G M_b/H_Lam^2)^(1/3):
    d log R_0 / d log M_b        = +1/3 exactly   -> d log R_0/d log Upsilon = (1/3) x (stellar share of M_b)
       stellar share of M_b(LG) = 0.858  =>  d log R_0/d log Upsilon = +0.286
    d log R_0 / d log g_ext      = (1/3) d log nu/d log e_N x d log e_N/d log g_ext
       canonical  d log R_0/d log g_ext = -0.3203   (nu falls as e^-1/2, so the answer is weakly sensitive to the external-field estimate)
       alt        d log R_0/d log g_ext = -0.3224   (nu falls as e^-1/2, so the answer is weakly sensitive to the external-field estimate)
    canonical  footing/branch spread: EFE-quenched 1.06 Mpc vs isolated 1.90 Mpc = 0.25 dex
    alt        footing/branch spread: EFE-quenched 1.08 Mpc vs isolated 1.89 Mpc = 0.24 dex

  MUTATION CONTROLS
    M1 a_0 x 0.1  : isolated-MOND R_0 ->   1.214 Mpc (vs 1.899 at the true a_0)
    M1 a_0 x 10   : isolated-MOND R_0 ->   0.612 Mpc (vs 1.899 at the true a_0)
  [PASS] K02.8 MUTATION: scaling a_0 by 10 must move the framework's prediction.  R_scale goes as a_0^(1/4)/H_Lam ~ a_0^(-3/4), partly offset because x_ta rises with H_Lam t_0; net, a 10x wrong a_0 must move R_0 by more than 0.3 dex, and the estimator is therefore not an a_0-blind fixed point   (a_0 x 10 moves the isolated prediction by more than 0.3 dex)
    M2 shuffling V_LG among the same galaxies: R_0 -> median 0.20 Mpc, 16-84% [-8.73, 13.55] -- the Hubble slope is destroyed
  [PASS] K02.9 MUTATION: shuffling which galaxy carries which velocity must destroy the measurement.  If the shuffled R_0 distribution contained the real value tightly, the fit would be a property of the marginal distributions rather than of the pairing   (shuffled median 0.20 Mpc with an 16-84 width of 22.28 Mpc vs the real 0.88)

==============================================================================================================================
7. BUG-PATTERN AUDIT
==============================================================================================================================
  (1) TOTAL vs ENCLOSED mass.  The turnaround radius is OUTSIDE the whole system, so the TOTAL baryonic mass
      is the correct one here -- the opposite of the usual trap, and stated so it is not fixed by mistake.
      Checked: the membership cut takes everything within 1.2 Mpc of the barycentre, inside the measured R_0's
      collapsing region, and adding the 0.7-1.2 Mpc shell changes M_b by less than 3%.
  (2) SPHERICAL formula on a DISC.  Not applicable: at Mpc scales the Local Group is a two-body point mass, and
      the collapse integral is spherical by construction.  The two-body correction IS a real caveat and is
      recorded in the verdict rather than modelled.
  (3) An aperture on a SADDLE.  The LG barycentre is a maximum of the potential's source, not a saddle; the
      saddle between MW and M31 is at ~0.35 Mpc, inside the excluded region (the fit starts at 0.7 Mpc).
  (4) A covariance in the wrong index order.  No covariance is used; errors are galaxy bootstraps.
  (5) A trivial correlation from joint-fit degeneracy.  R_0 comes from distances and velocities; M_b comes from
      K-band light and HI fluxes.  The two share the distance scale (both scale with D), which is the one real
      coupling: R_0 ~ D and M_b ~ D^2, so d log(R_0 pred)/d log D = 2/3 against d log(R_0 obs)/d log D = 1.
      A 10% distance-scale error therefore moves the RATIO by only 0.014 dex, not by 0.10.

==============================================================================================================================
VERDICT -- ITEM 80 / CANDIDATE k02
==============================================================================================================================
  THE ITEM AS WRITTEN IS REFUTED.  Its prediction was the isolated deep-MOND turnaround radius
  R_0 = x_ta (G M_b a_0)^(1/4)/H_Lam.  Measured against the Local Group's own zero-velocity surface it
  over-predicts by a factor 2.1 (canonical) / 2.1 (alt).
  THE REASON IS STRUCTURAL, NOT ACCIDENTAL, and it is the transferable finding: at a turnaround radius the
  system's own field has by definition fallen to H_Lam^2 R_0, which is 30-50x below the external field of
  large-scale structure.  EVERY zero-velocity surface in the Local Volume is deep in the external-field
  regime.  The isolated deep-MOND branch can never be the right one for this observable.
  WHAT SURVIVES, and it is a different and better statement than the item's: with the external field measured
  from the group's own peculiar velocity, the framework is quasi-Newtonian at R_0 with G -> nu(e_N)(1-L/3) G,
  and the Local Group's zero-velocity radius follows with no dark matter and no fitted parameter.  The
  discriminating content is then a CORRELATION nothing in LambdaCDM produces: M_dyn/M_b at the zero-velocity
  surface must fall as the group's peculiar velocity rises, roughly as v_pec^(-1/2), where LambdaCDM gives the
  same 1/f_b for every group regardless of its motion.  One system cannot test a correlation; this needs the
  10-15 Local Volume groups with measured R_0 and the CMB-frame peculiar velocity of each.
  NOT KEPLER-GRADE ON ONE SYSTEM.  Promoted to the list as a two-parameter correlation test, not as a law.

